@startuml Funding Models Comparison

skinparam backgroundColor #f5f6f1
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #c7cbb4
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #dbdec9
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam noteBorderColor #c7cbb4
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #f3e8d2
skinparam dividerBackgroundColor #e4efe6
skinparam dividerBorderColor #2f6f5b

title Funding Models — Prefunded Wallet vs. Atomic Pull-and-Pay

== Model A: Prefunded Wallet (assumed default) ==

actor       "Merchant"            as M
participant "Payout API"          as API
database    "Wallet Ledger\n(Postgres)" as WL
database    "Payout Ledger\n(Postgres)" as PL
queue       "Kafka"               as K
participant "Disbursement\nWorker" as DW
participant "Partner Rail"        as Rail

note over M, Rail #e4efe6 : Step 0 — Merchant tops up wallet BEFORE calling POST /payouts.\nThis is a separate flow (POST /wallets/topup), not shown here.

M -> API  : POST /payouts\n{ amount, beneficiary }

API -> WL : BEGIN\nSELECT balance FOR UPDATE
alt Sufficient balance
  API -> WL : UPDATE wallet SET balance = balance - amount\nINSERT wallet_ledger (debit entry)
  API -> PL : INSERT payout (status=PENDING)\nCOMMIT
  API -> K  : publish payout.created
  API --> M : 202 Accepted\n{ payout_id, status: PENDING }
  note right of API : Funds already Boku's to move.\nPayout acceptance is clean —\none failure surface (disbursement only).
  K -> DW   : consume payout.created
  DW -> Rail: submit disbursement
  Rail --> DW: settled / failed
  DW -> PL  : UPDATE status = SETTLED | FAILED
else Insufficient balance
  API --> M : 422 Unprocessable\n{ error_code: INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS }
  note right of API : Synchronous rejection —\nno payout record created.
end

== Model B: Atomic Pull-and-Pay (alternative) ==

actor       "Merchant"            as M2
participant "Payout API"          as API2
participant "Payment Rail\n(Debit Mandate)" as PayRail
database    "Payout Ledger"       as PL2
queue       "Kafka"               as K2
participant "Disbursement\nWorker" as DW2
participant "Partner Rail"        as Rail2

note over M2, Rail2 #fff3e0 : No pre-funding step — caller holds a Boku direct debit mandate.\nOne API call triggers both money movements.

M2 -> API2 : POST /payouts\n{ amount, beneficiary }
API2 -> PL2 : INSERT payout (status=PENDING)
API2 --> M2 : 202 Accepted\n{ payout_id, status: PENDING }

API2 -> PayRail : debit caller's account\n(async, via mandate)

note right of PayRail #f3e8d2 : Two failure surfaces now:\n1. Pull from caller fails\n2. Disbursement to beneficiary fails\nEach needs its own error state\nand reconciliation path.

alt Pull succeeds
  PayRail --> API2 : funds received
  API2 -> K2 : publish payout.funded
  K2 -> DW2  : consume payout.funded
  DW2 -> Rail2 : submit disbursement
  Rail2 --> DW2 : settled / failed
  DW2 -> PL2 : UPDATE status = SETTLED | FAILED
else Pull fails
  PayRail --> API2 : insufficient funds / mandate revoked
  API2 -> PL2 : UPDATE status = FAILED\nfailure_reason = PULL_FAILED
  note right of PL2 : Nothing paid to beneficiary.\nBut a payout record exists — \ncaller must be notified the\npull itself failed, not just settlement.
end

@enduml
